Implement independent bounded scalar algebra replay. Export Certificate {version:u32,domain:String,start:Expr,end:Expr,steps:Vec<ReplayStep>,nonzero_assumptions:Vec<Expr>}, ReplayStep {before:Expr,after:Expr,rule:Rule}, Rule::{PolynomialIdentity,RationalIdentity}, replay(&Certificate,&mut Budget)->Result<ReplayReport>. Report steps_checked, conditional_domain Vec<String>, statement, formal_proof=false. Export CERTIFICATE_VERSION and SCALAR_DOMAIN. Bind exact version/convention. Reject empty certificates. Validate all inputs with one Budget; hard depth cap 128 and aggregate bytes/nodes before recursive AST calls. Canonical syntax only links start/steps/end; independent exact sparse BTreeMap monomial-to-BigC expansion checks identities. Never call production Polynomial or RationalFunction normalization. Reuse trusted BigC checked arithmetic. Polynomial rule forbids quotients. Rational rule recursively builds uncancelled numerator/denominator pairs and cross multiplies only with every syntactic denominator explicitly assumed nonzero, including nested and zero-masked poles. Validate all supplied assumptions including unused ones, reject normalized zero assumptions and denominators even if assumed. Report assumptions as conditional, never established. Reject OrderedProduct/operators/tensors/binders even scalar-valued. Preflight degree, terms, aggregate input bytes, map growth, dense crossproduct sizes, coefficient work and comparisons before growth; conservative rejection allowed. Limits bound declared work, not OS memory/time. Exact independent fixtures and tamper negatives must cover wrong steps, assumptions, chain/end forgery, conventions, unsupported AST and budgets. No floating witnesses or Lean/formal QFT proof claims. No provider calls.
